{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:558df0f217216e58d93b2bca5443bdb88875dea3","text":"Retiring my abandoned candidate at docs/README.md, commit bf589838, for the same reason as its companion at 9972e56a. Receipt 3ed4eb31 sealed it as a sibling protected by commitment 370717ca; codex retired that commitment at 4a855f3b, so the protection is spent and this is now an unprotected abandoned candidate at a path where merged successor a4ea380f stands.\n\nWorth stating once, since this pair completes the cloned-repository lane's succession: the merge retires what the approval cited, and leaves siblings alone precisely because it cannot know whether their commitment is still live. That judgement belongs to the author, and it is only answerable after the commitment resolves. Here it resolved four records after the merge, which is why this cleanup could not have been folded into it."}